{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Let there be a firmament.</b> Let the firmament grow firm — for even though the heavens were created on day one, they were still moist, and on the second they congealed from the rebuke of the Holy One, blessed be He, when He said 'Let there be a firmament.' And this is what is written (Job 26): ״עַמּוּדֵי שָׁמַיִם יְרוֹפָפוּ״ — all the first day, and on the second they were astounded from His rebuke, like a person who is astounded and stands still from the rebuke of the one reproving him." "<b>In the midst of the waters.</b> In the middle of the waters — that there is a separation between the upper waters and the firmament just as between the firmament and the waters that are upon the earth. From this you learn that they are suspended by the utterance of the King."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:03.762721907Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}